        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_742"/>
        <dc:title>Replacement Patterns of Beech and Sugar Maple in Warren Woods, Michigan</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Factors responsible for patterns of canopy tree replacement were studied for 22 yr in Warren Woods, Michigan, USA, an old-growth forest codominated by American beech (Fagus grandifolia) and sugar maple (Acer saccharum). Our goal was to distinguish among four hypotheses: autogenic succession, allogenic succession, autogenic coexistence, and allogenic coexistence.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>06/1996</dc:date>
