        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_2296"/>
        <dc:title>Beech regeneration research: From ecological to silvicultural aspects</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>This review describes key regeneration characteristics of the genus Fagus as represented by its four most prominent species: F. crenata (F.c.), F. grandifolia (F.g.), F. orientalis (F.o.) and F. sylvatica (F.s.). Similarities and differences in the relevant life phases of these species are identiﬁed. Those are related to natural disturbance regimes and synecological peculiarities of the forests where they grow, thereby establishing a basis for evaluating the likely outcome of different silvicultural measures.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>5/2010</dc:date>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:shortTitle>Beech regeneration research</z:shortTitle>
        <z:libraryCatalog>DOI.org (Crossref)</z:libraryCatalog>
